<title>NETHERLANDS: ABN AMRO silent on MGAM buy-out reports.</title>
<headline>ABN AMRO silent on MGAM buy-out reports.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch bank ABN AMRO NV said on Tuesday it had no comment on British newspaper reports it had planned to back a management buy-out of Morgan Grenfell Asset Management's (MGAM) British pension fund business.</p>
<p>&quot;We have said everything we have to say (on the matter),&quot; bank spokesman Tanno Massar told Reuters.</p>
<p>The reports suggested the buy-out would have been led by Nicola Horlick, the fund manager who resigned from MGAM last week after being suspended for an alleged breach of contract.</p>
<p>ABN AMRO has denied reports it tried to poach Horlick and her MGAM team to bolster its British fund management activities.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
